  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a variational quantum feature deep neural network (QFDNN) using a UU† encoding method and a small variational circuit (3 qubits) evaluated on two financial datasets. On a 500-sample credit card fraud dataset the model achieved 0.822 accuracy, while classical methods reached up to 1.000; on a loan prediction dataset it achieved 0.744 accuracy versus 0.854 for logistic regression. All experiments were conducted on a simulator with injected noise models rather than real quantum hardware.",
